Leaks the inner layers of the compose-middleware closure onion: each
layer captures the downstream `next` box, and the outer-handler free done in
httpd-free/httpd-async-free cannot reach the inner boxes from C (the box is
opaque and the env layout is not a stable ABI). Intentional, bounded,
process-lifetime leak -- one box per middleware layer. Fix tracked in
docs/httpd-middleware-chain-drop-plan.md (reified server-owned chain); kept
marked until that lands.
